(a) nukta.h against Python's unicodedata (Unicode 15.1.0)
    11 rows (NUKTA_LEN 11); the code points of U+0900-U+097F whose NFD is a consonant and U+093C: 11                 ok
    the rows are exactly those code points                                                                           ok
    every row is the NFD pair of its letter: base + U+093C                                                           ok
    NUKTA_BYTE is 0xE9, the byte of U+093C in unicode.h                                                              ok
    every base letter has a byte in unicode.h                                                                        ok
    the nfc mark of a row is 1 if and only if NFC composes the pair (U+0929, U+0931, U+0934)                         ok
    the other eight (U+0958-U+095F) are the composition exclusions: NFC leaves their pair decomposed                 ok
    only U+0929 and U+0931 have a row in unicode.h; the other nine have none                                         ok
    the default NUKTA_FORM is 0, asis: the converters write what they always wrote                                   ok
    D3, the byte that ISCII gives ZHA (U+0934), is not a byte of unicode.h: the layer does not take it (section 15.7, C7) ok
(b) uni2acii in the three forms
    form asis: the single code point is written as 11 of 11 expected, consonant + nukta as 11 of 11                  ok
    form nfc : the single code point is written as 11 of 11 expected, consonant + nukta as 11 of 11                  ok
    form nfd : the single code point is written as 11 of 11 expected, consonant + nukta as 11 of 11                  ok
    asis: the nine have one spelling in ACII (single code point = pair); U+0929 and U+0931 have two (C7 and C6 E9, D0 and CF E9): 9 of 11 ok
    nfd: all eleven have one spelling, the consonant and E9: 11 of 11                                                ok
    nfc: all eleven have one spelling (C7 and D0 for U+0929 and U+0931, the consonant and E9 for the other nine): 11 of 11 ok
    patch 0001 alone wrote the low byte of the nine and the table byte of the two: 11 of 11                          ok
