(h) the edge cases
    a consonant at the end of the stream, no newline                         C6                       -> asis U+0928 ok
    a consonant before a newline                                             C6 LF                    -> asis U+0928 LF ok
    a consonant before another consonant                                     C6 B3                    -> asis U+0928 U+0915 ok
    NA NA E9: only the second has a nukta                                    C6 C6 E9                 -> asis U+0928 U+0928 U+093C | nfc U+0928 U+0929 ok
    NA E9 E9: the second E9 stands alone                                     C6 E9 E9                 -> asis U+0928 U+093C U+093C | nfc U+0929 U+093C ok
    E9 alone, and E9 after a newline                                         E9 LF E9                 -> asis U+093C LF U+093C ok
    NNNA (the byte C7) + E9: the byte with its own row is not a consonant    C7 E9                    -> asis U+0929 U+093C | nfd U+0928 U+093C U+093C ok
    NA, newline, E9: the newline ends the held byte                          C6 LF E9                 -> asis U+0928 LF U+093C ok
    NA, halant, E9: ISCII's E8 E9, not a nukta of NA                         C6 E8 E9                 -> asis U+0928 U+094D U+093C ok
    NA, vowel sign AA, E9: a vowel sign between                              C6 DA E9                 -> asis U+0928 U+093E U+093C ok
    RA E9 and LLA E9                                                         CF E9 D2 E9              -> asis U+0930 U+093C U+0933 U+093C | nfc U+0931 U+0934 ok
    KA E9: a composition exclusion, a pair in every form                     B3 E9                    -> asis U+0915 U+093C ok
    C7 and D0 alone: the two letters that have a byte                        C7 D0                    -> asis U+0929 U+0931 | nfd U+0928 U+093C U+0930 U+093C ok
    an empty input gives the byte order mark and nothing else                                                        ok
    both converters print their usage line when called with one file name                                            ok
    NA at the end of the stream: the consonant that waited is written            -> asis C6                          ok
    NA + nukta at the end of the stream                                          -> asis C6 E9 | nfc C7              ok
    NA, newline, nukta: the newline ends the wait                                -> asis C6 0A E9                    ok
    NA NA nukta: only the second has a nukta                                     -> asis C6 C6 E9 | nfc C6 C7        ok
    NA + nukta + nukta: the second nukta stands alone                            -> asis C6 E9 E9 | nfc C7 E9        ok
    RA + nukta, LLA + nukta                                                      -> asis CF E9 D2 E9 | nfc D0 D2 E9  ok
    NA + halant + nukta: not composed in any form                                -> asis C6 E8 E9                    ok
    NA + vowel sign AA + nukta                                                   -> asis C6 DA E9                    ok
    KA + nukta: a composition exclusion                                          -> asis B3 E9                       ok
    U+0929 and U+0931                                                            -> asis C7 D0 | nfd C6 E9 CF E9     ok
    U+0934 and U+095C: written as the consonant and E9 in every form             -> asis D2 E9 BF E9                 ok
    a consonant, then a low-byte character (U+00E9), then a nukta: the é is not the nukta -> asis C6 E9 E9           ok
